+    // Do not put types in their own units. WebKit's cmake turns them on for
+    // clang (Source/cmake/WebKitCompilerFlags.cmake) and notes right there
+    // that they break Linux distribution debuginfo generation - it already
+    // disables them for gcc for that reason. They break it for clang too:
+    // type units are comdat, the linker keeps one copy of each and drops the
+    // rest, but the .debug_str_offsets slots for the strings only a dropped
+    // unit named stay behind. debugedit rewrites that table entry by entry
+    // and asserts on the first slot no unit refers to any more
+    // ("string_find_entry: Assertion `ret != NULL' failed"), so rpm cannot
+    // split a debuginfo package off the executable at all. In a release
+    // build the type units are 14 MB of 437 MB of .debug_info, so this costs
+    // very little. WebKit prepends its own flags to CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS and
+    // these are appended, so this one wins.
+    if (cfg.unix && !cfg.darwin) optFlags.push("-fno-debug-types-section");
     if (cfg.lto) optFlags.push("-flto=thin");
